{
  "id": 241419714,
  "iid": 11607,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "SNMP: Don't check the tvb length on a fragmented packet",
  "description": "If the packet is fragmented (e.g., IPv4 defragmentation was\ndisabled) or an error packet (ICMP truncated payload), don't\nreject the packet just because the length is shorter than\nindicated in the BER length field.\n\nInstead, continue to dissect it, which will put SNMP in the\ntree and dissect as much as possible before putting a\nFragmentBoundsError expert info in the tree with a message\nhinting to turn on reassembly if necessary.\n\nFix #19246",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-08-05T00:16:04.582Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-08-05T22:05:43.415Z",
