  "discussions_data": [
    {
      "id": "084b46329dd38962d1d80ee62e2af0a57e090a94",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1501593715,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Well, the SNMP ports are configurable, so it should 'get out of the way' if it sees this problem this early in the packet. The additional checks are okay, the comment should be changed to this effect, IMHO.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2398962,
            "username": "JaapKeuter",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jaap Keuter",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/722b0c520542a23cb8f8ea7070a45c88f9e9214dc700ac151e419e9649e0304e?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/JaapKeuter"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-08-05T06:39:04.976Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-08-05T06:39:04.976Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 241419714,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 11607,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "774c1a456383163a3081fc04d3b62f86f9938a4f",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1501608026,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Sure, I have no problem changing.\n\nA rare but possible problem for using this as heuristics is that `get_ber_identifier()` and `get_ber_length()` can throw exceptions (and in the case of either the long form of the length (8.1.3.5) or indefinite length (8.1.3.6), we don't know the length of the supposed length tag without parsing, so it's hard to test the captured length outside that.)\n\nThere should probably be a \"get BER identifier/length but don't throw an exception, return a value on failure\" function (the BER dissector itself uses TRY..EXCEPT blocks in a few places due to this).",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-08-05T07:43:16.999Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-08-05T07:43:16.999Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 241419714,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 11607,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "660940fe011f9b8fb5fca85cf0d05b77351b523b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1501609337,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I also am a little skeptical that the \"random data after a PDU added by some other tool (#3684)\" case is really more common than \"GSO results in multiple PDUs in a datagram,\" but someone did complain about the former and we don't have an issue yet filed with the latter.",
